Subject: Candidate Seal and Independent Review Feature Slice

@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Candidate_Seal_And_Independent_Review.sop
@ [matrix] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\CandidateSealAndIndependentReview_Requirement_Matrix.sop

& [SliceIdentity] is Phase3C formation
  + [slice_uuid] is 4e066b9a-bbe0-4071-8b27-21b2a8ecac74
  + [status] is formation_complete_implementation_blocked
  + [depends_on] is CandidateWorkspaceAdmission complete and BoundedCandidateMutation formed

& [ContiguousPurpose] is immutable evidence and independent non-promotional judgment
  + [inside] is quiescence, physical seal, separate reconstruction and supervisor tests, independent review, typed faults, and Phase3D evidence handoff
  + [outside] is Phase3B implementation, live candidate mutation, cleanup, current-authority signing, Git-history mutation, and promotion

& [ActivationPath] is dependency ordered
  + [step_1] is stabilize and fixture-test strict schemas and state transitions
  + [step_2] is prove target-host quiescence and full inventory grammar
  + [step_3] is prove admitted seal-root atomicity, durability, collision, and permissions
  + [step_4] is prove exact reconstruction and a separately contained test runner
  + [step_5] is prove independent review and Phase3D handoff boundaries
  + [step_6] is preserve findings as reconciliation source and renew authority
  + [step_7] is only then implement one minimal disposable proof
  - never: skip from formation to physical sealing or test execution
